{
	// ## Why this file exists
	//
	// `npm run check` runs svelte-check against the repo's root tsconfig, whose `include` comes
	// from the generated `.svelte-kit/tsconfig.json` — and that list is `src/**`, `test/**`,
	// `tests/**`. `e2e/**` is in NONE of them. Playwright transpiles specs with esbuild, which
	// does not type-check. So until now a genuine type error in a spec shipped silently: it
	// would either blow up at run time or, worse, quietly assert the wrong thing.
	//
	// Found while reviewing the a11y.spec.ts change in this same branch, which added a
	// `page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion })` call — exactly the kind of edit where a wrong
	// literal type would have gone unnoticed.
	//
	// `types: ["node"]` because the generated config targets the browser/Svelte environment and
	// specs reach for Node globals (`process.env`) that are otherwise unresolved.
	"extends": "../tsconfig.json",
	"compilerOptions": {
		"noEmit": true,
		"types": ["node"]
	},
	"include": ["**/*.ts"]
}
